Expand an arbitrary ket as $\ket{A}=\sum_i \alpha_i\ket{i}.$ The coefficients are not mysterious. Multiply from the left by $\bra{j}$: $\begin{aligned}
\braket{j}{A}
 &=\sum_i\alpha_i\braket{j}{i} \\
 &=\sum_i\alpha_i\delta_{ji}
 =\alpha_j.\end{aligned}$ Thus $\alpha_i=\braket{i}{A}.$ The $i$-th component is the projection of $\ket{A}$ onto the $i$-th basis direction.

