p.src:
Begin with the upper diagonal entry: $\begin{aligned}
\bra{u}\sigma_x\ket{u}
 &=\frac12(\bra{r}+\bra{l})\sigma_x(\ket{r}+\ket{l})\\
 &=\frac12(\bra{r}+\bra{l})(\ket{r}-\ket{l})\\
 &=0.\end{aligned}$ The right and left states are orthonormal, so the two diagonal terms cancel and the cross terms vanish. The same calculation with $\ket{d}$ gives $\bra{d}\sigma_x\ket{d}=0.$ At this point two zeros do not mean the operator vanishes; they tell us to look off the diagonal.

